Subject: drivers: flash: spi_nor: bound the WIP status poll with a timeout

spi_nor_wait_until_ready() polls the status register in a while(true) loop that
exits only on a SPI read error or when WIP clears. On a transient SPI glitch that
leaves the status read stuck at WIP=1, it busy-spins forever, blocking the caller
until the IWDG resets the MCU mid erase/program. Observed on divecan_jr's
W25Q512JV: the 0xF278 whole-chip mass erase and the factory-restore copy hang at
random deep offsets, so the erase never reaches the NVS partition and the restore
leaves slot1 incomplete. Add a 10 s deadline so a stuck-busy becomes a
recoverable -ETIMEDOUT the caller can retry/skip. A worst-case single block erase
is ~2 s and the app never issues a full-chip CE (it erases in 256 KiB chunks), so
no legitimate operation approaches the bound. Applied automatically at configure
time by Firmware/CMakeLists.txt; git apply tolerates this preamble.

diff --git a/drivers/flash/spi_nor.c b/drivers/flash/spi_nor.c
--- a/drivers/flash/spi_nor.c
+++ b/drivers/flash/spi_nor.c
@@ -525,6 +525,17 @@ static int spi_nor_wait_until_ready(const struct device *dev, k_timeout_t poll_d

 	ARG_UNUSED(poll_delay);

+	/* Bound the WIP poll. This loop otherwise has NO timeout: on a transient
+	 * SPI glitch that leaves the status read stuck at WIP=1, it busy-spins
+	 * forever, blocking the caller until the IWDG resets the MCU mid
+	 * erase/program (HW-observed on divecan_jr's W25Q512JV: the 0xF278 mass
+	 * erase and factory-restore copy hang at random deep offsets). A worst-case
+	 * single block erase is ~2 s, so a 10 s cap catches a true hang with wide
+	 * margin and returns a recoverable -ETIMEDOUT instead. The app erases in
+	 * 256 KiB chunks (never a full-chip CE), so no legitimate operation here
+	 * approaches this bound. */
+	int64_t wip_deadline = k_uptime_get() + 10000;
+
 	while (true) {
 		/* If flag status register is present, check it rather than the standard
 		 * status register since it allows better error detection. Also, some devices
@@ -567,6 +578,11 @@ static int spi_nor_wait_until_ready(const struct device *dev, k_timeout_t poll_d
 				break;
 			}
 		}
+		if (k_uptime_get() >= wip_deadline) {
+			LOG_ERR("spi_nor: WIP poll timed out (stuck busy)");
+			ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
+			break;
+		}
 #ifdef CONFIG_SPI_NOR_SLEEP_WHILE_WAITING_UNTIL_READY
 		/* Don't monopolise the CPU while waiting for ready */
 		k_sleep(poll_delay);
